detail:
Bounds substring-matches the model root's direct children against three token lists: building ['MainBuildingModel','Storey__'], ground ['LandscapeEnvironment'], ignore ['OrbitHelperCube'].

VV's loader names each child group by its category key (VVM/15__ModelLoader/Na__ModelLoader__MultiModel.js:857). The keys come from three regexes (:145-148):
- current exports: ValeVision__<Category>, e.g. MainBuildingModel__Existing/Proposed/ProposedDoors, LandscapeEnvironment, SiteBoundaries;
- storey exports: Storey__<Storey>__<Element>;
- every older __Layer-XX__ export: one ValeVision__LegacyModel bucket.

No VV path produces 'Landscape' or 'Walls' categories, so TV's Bounds PORT NOTE (TVM/47/...Bounds__.js:47-50) and plan line 133 are stale. TV's tokens match VV's current and storey exports. A legacy single-bucket project matches no building token and falls back to TV's own usedFallback (the whole model minus ground and ignored groups): a degrade, not a failure. Not verified on a loaded VV model.

TV styles nested LineworkModifier owners in the Layout Editor through three pieces:
- a ModelLayers config group (Layer__CategoryKey TrueVision__LineworkModifier__*, SketchUp tags 76-79, Group__AlwaysShow);
- Viewport2d__Frame importing Na__PlCfg__GetLineworkModifiers for widths;
- Viewport2d__Linework treating modifier keys as never top-level.
Without these, VV segments would carry owner keys with no style row and draw in the fallback style.

VV's GLBs come from the same exporter. ValeVision Cloud Sync calls Na__TrueVision__GlbBuilderUtility through 04__Plugin__SyncFeatures/03__GlbExportBridge/Na__ValeVisionCloudSync__GlbExportBridge__.rb:57, and that builder writes nested LineworkModifier nodes (Na__TrueVision__GlbBuilder__EngineCore__LineworkModelHandling__.rb:15, 76). Whether Vale models actually carry tags 76-79 is still unverified.

